cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these derived tables, please cite the archived release and the article."
title: "Human Skin Permeability Prediction by Machine Learning for Transdermal Drug Delivery — analysis code and derived data"
abstract: >-
  Analysis pipeline and derived tables for a pooled reanalysis of two open human skin-permeation
  databases (732 permeability records, 327 compounds). Includes the held-out split and
  cross-validation fold assignments, the accumulated local effects and bootstrap bands, the
  200-split held-out distribution, the corrected fold-wise tests, the permutation and matching
  analyses of skin layer, the mixed-effects variance decomposition, the ionization analysis and
  the ATC verification table.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sanghyunn82-creator/skin-permeability-kp"
version: 1.0.0
